ch intratumoral bacteria modulate ICI efficacy. Mechanisms include: 1) Direct immune checkpoint regulation (Fn upregulating PD-L1 via Dps protein); 2) Metabolic modulation (Fn-derived succinate suppressing cGAS-IFN-β pathway; L. reuteri-derived I3A activating AhR to boost CD8+ T cell IFN-γ production); 3) Immune cell recruitment/polarization (recruiting MDSCs or Tregs via chemokines like CXCL1/CXCL8); 4) STING pathway activation (Bifidobacterium activating STING to convert non-responders to responders). Also describes how engineered bacteria or probiotics can reverse resistance.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::44a2fa1a46e0fdd814aa8881\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on *intratumoral* bacteria, which may differ from the *gut* microbiome specified in the user's query. While there are links (e.g., translocation), they are distinct ecological niches. Use with caution when generalizing gut-specific mechanisms to intra-tumor effects.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1d685375e8722d8afbd25341\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic claims are based on preclinical models (mice/cell lines). Human clinical evidence is often correlative or from small cohorts. Do not overstate causal certainty for human outcomes.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07d1a824dccc99281c19dc7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes context-dependency; the same bacterium can have opposite effects in different cancer types or immune contexts. Avoid universal statements about specific taxa without specifying the tumor type and immune status.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07f1e5183847229ad8b2e864\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7e6154be7d1862fb8f12\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f7ea40020efdf4450b0c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-44244ea1ee064f912ccc\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-209c537883b93c0e9089\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d5ca696c6dd975cca57920d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b4f0d0ef1f78fb08a8aa82e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1fe8cbfe8386b8f65a1b468\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用主题式综合叙述方法。首先按疾病类别（代谢疾病、肿瘤、病原体感染）分别梳理微生物组的作用机制（代谢调节、免疫调节、基因毒性等）；其次，针对每类疾病，对比分析不同层级的干预手段（从非特异性FMT/益生菌到特异性工程菌）；最后，讨论工程菌作为下一代益生菌在体内传感、治疗和生物 containment 方面的技术路线及局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c0d91dd32d0f6a42456ab635\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组在代谢、肿瘤和感染三大领域作用机制的系统性框架，特别强调了工程菌在精准医疗中的多样化角色（传感、治疗、诊断）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，其结论依赖于引用的原始研究，未提供新的实验数据；对工程菌临床转化的描述主要基于作者对现有文献的综合，实际临床成功率（如SYNB1020的失败案例）提示了当前技术的局限性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dabcf19be6b96384e19654a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"代谢疾病模型中\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物组通过分泌短链脂肪酸（SCFA）、次级胆汁酸和TMAO等代谢物调节宿主代谢；同时，肠道屏障功能障碍导致的低度全身性炎症是代谢疾病的重要驱动因素。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d30edb082bd96350ff790439\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肿瘤治疗背景下\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定肠道菌群组成（如Roseburia hominis富集、Prevotella/Bacteroides比例高）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）的良好响应相关；而某些菌群（如Veillonella parvula）与非响应相关。微生物组还通过ROS产生、药物代谢（如5-FU）和TNF激活影响化疗效果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::218c82f1989acf02ccf45fb4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"病原体感染背景下\",\n          \"finding\": \"共生微生物组通过营养竞争、抗菌素分泌（直接途径）和激活宿主免疫/产生抗菌肽（间接途径）提供定植抗力。工程菌可设计为感知病原体信号（如CAI-1）并释放毒素或酶进行靶向清除。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69b768ac929026456690484f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76f1ac5be0a9e65e1a52ad49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"阐明共生微生物组在多种重大疾病（代谢病、癌症、感染）中的病理生理机制，并评估基于微生物组的干预策略（尤其是工程菌）的临床潜力与应用现状。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b1cd7df36e01bfb86b40ca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类共生微生物组（包括肠道、皮肤、阴道等部位）及其在代谢疾病、肿瘤和病原体感染中的医学应用，重点涵盖传统干预手段（益生菌、FMT）与合成生物学工程菌的应用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1b84f22d3980cb93e7a6334\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述旨在总结共生微生物组在特定疾病中的作用机制及工程菌在疾病预防、检测和治疗的最新进展。文章首先回顾了微生物组通过代谢产物（如SCFA、胆汁酸、TMAO）和炎症调节影响宿主代谢的机制，随后探讨了微生物组在肿瘤发生、转移及治疗反应（特别是免疫检查点抑制剂ICIs和化疗）中的双向作用，最后阐述了微生物组通过定植抗力抵抗病原体感染的机制。在此基础上，文章系统梳理了从非靶向干预（抗生素、饮食、FMT、益生菌）到靶向干预（工程菌作为传感器、治疗剂或诊断工具）的策略演变，并指出了工程菌临床转化面临的挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::990eeee11679939276207321\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章指出肿瘤组织（如乳腺癌、胶质母细胞瘤）中存在独特的微生物组成，且肿瘤内细菌可能随癌细胞转移至转移灶，促进肿瘤生长。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::90f40cdb44ea31e2e1a5b575\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章引用Shiao et al. (2021)的研究，指出肿瘤内细菌对放疗后的抗肿瘤免疫反应是必要的，而肿瘤内真菌通过Dectin-1受体抑制抗肿瘤免疫反应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::820a381a4ff7239d71a1800c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章提到SYNB1020在动物模型成功但在I期临床试验中未达预期，归因于宿主-微生物互作的复杂性及反馈抑制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::81ba7ad99d2b68647f51f92c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些发现主要基于回顾性队列研究和动物模型，且涉及多种癌症类型（包括胃肠道癌），需结合具体实体瘤类型进行细化。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的微生物标志物：指出Roseburia hominis富集与ICI响应正相关，Veillonella parvula与非响应相关；提到基于细菌分类群的预测模型（如Prevotella/Bacteroides比例）能准确预测PD-1/PD-L1单药治疗反应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ba339e0712a59351affb82d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制研究多在小鼠模型中进行，人体内的确切通路仍需更多临床验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了微生物组增强ICI疗效的机制：口服活体乳酸杆菌可增加Lactobacillus murinus和Bacteroides uniformis丰度，通过cGAS/STING轴激活树突状细胞IFN-β产生，进而促进CD8+ T细胞浸润肿瘤；微生物组缺失会削弱CpG-ODN和anti-IL-10R诱导的TNF表达和抗肿瘤效果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c1f2cea1b4ca1341506f1933\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要针对特定化疗药物（奥沙利铂、5-FU），不一定适用于所有化疗方案。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了微生物组影响化疗疗效的机制：微生物核糖核苷酸代谢影响氟尿嘧啶（5-FU）疗效；微生物介导的ROS产生依赖于是氧化铂的抗肿瘤效应；微生物组调控TNF表达影响联合免疫治疗效果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a53346d912c074c14a042c14\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"目前主要处于临床前小鼠模型阶段，尚未成为标准临床实践。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了工程菌作为增强ICI疗效的新机制：工程菌携带同步裂解电路（SLC）递送PD-L1或CTLA-4纳米抗体，或在肿瘤局部表达GM-CSF，从而系统性激活T细胞反应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9461ad2e6421ce17b99301b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述将代谢疾病、肿瘤和感染并列讨论，需注意区分不同疾病背景下微生物组的具体作用机制，避免混淆。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c417190a6aba285b31bc53e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关于ICI响应的微生物标志物多为相关性研究，因果关系的确定需谨慎，且不同癌症类型的响应菌群可能存在差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6a1e20f9c24f8d9d996dcdee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"工程菌的大部分应用仍处于临床前阶段，将其机制外推到当前临床实践时需明确标注其实验性质。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6441414f0a6b8411d9a5bc5d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0132\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-edcd953058d1d5fa5081\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-57c86dec56d8ae37b5be\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1665125cc52bd142aafc9e1a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::406641079f60298daf18306f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b401c57697656fea4f657072\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b6917c39e00872cf55a398e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 模型构建：工程化B16-F10、LLC1和MC-38细胞系稳定表达SFB抗原片段（SFB-3340），建立合成新抗原模拟肿瘤模型。 2. 体内干预：比较SFB定植（SFB+）与无菌（SFB-）小鼠在植入上述肿瘤后，接受或不接受抗PD-1抗体治疗的肿瘤生长情况。 3. 免疫表型分析：利用流式细胞术、MHC II类四聚体染色分析肿瘤浸润淋巴细胞（TILs）和肠道固有层（SILP）T细胞的亚群分布、转录因子表达（如RORγt, T-bet）及细胞因子分泌（IFN-γ, TNF, IL-17A）。 4. 克隆谱系追踪：结合scRNA-seq和scTCR-seq，配对分析SILP和肿瘤组织中CD4+ T细胞的TCR克隆型重叠，验证肠道到肿瘤的迁移关系。 5. 功能验证：使用Il17a-Cre;ROSA-LSL-DTA小鼠条件性清除IL-17A+ T细胞，评估其对ICB疗效及CD8+ T细胞功能的影响；进行过继转移实验追踪标记T细胞的命运。 6. 对照比较：使用诱导Foxp3+调节性T细胞的Helicobacter hepaticus (Hh)作为阴性对照，比较不同菌群诱导的T细胞程序对ICB疗效的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b1fb60c01983800f285d21e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道共生菌通过分子模拟增强ICB疗效的因果机制证据，定义了“肠道T_H17 -> 肿瘤ex-T_H17 -> CD8+ T细胞辅助”这一细胞通路。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代该机制在人类癌症患者中的普遍性或临床相关性；模型依赖于人工设计的抗原匹配，可能不反映自然感染或复杂菌群互作的全部情况；主要在小鼠模型中验证，外推到人体需谨慎。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d236cacc7f4c178f632ce164\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SFB定植 + 抗PD-1治疗 + SFB抗原表达肿瘤\",\n          \"finding\": \"显著抑制肿瘤生长并延长生存期，且产生持久的记忆样保护；单独SFB定植或单独抗PD-1治疗无此效果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1e3b15f8650c9346dfd46ae1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SFB定植小鼠的肿瘤组织\",\n          \"finding\": \"发现大量源自肠道的SFB特异性CD4+ T细胞浸润，其表型从肠道中的T_H17（IL-17A+）转变为肿瘤中的T_H1-like（IFN-γ+, TNF+, T-bet+, RORγt部分保留），即ex-T_H17细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2de560c549a1dd86781a5ce1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"scTCR-seq与谱系追踪\",\n          \"finding\": \"证实肿瘤中的ex-T_H17细胞与肠道SILP中的T_H17细胞共享相同的TCR克隆型，证明存在从肠道到肿瘤的迁移及表型重编程。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c337d8a90782fb8cd71b9556\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"条件性清除IL-17A+ T细胞\",\n          \"finding\": \"消除SFB诱导的IL-17A+ T细胞前体后，抗PD-1介导的肿瘤控制被完全取消，肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞招募和功能受损，表明ex-T_H17细胞是疗效的关键介质。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::935d44f812e517be8cabc35c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"H. hepaticus定植 + 抗PD-1治疗 + Hh抗原表达肿瘤\",\n          \"finding\": \"未观察到肿瘤生长抑制。虽然Hh特异性T细胞也迁移至肿瘤，但其维持Foxp3+调节性表型，缺乏促炎效应功能，无法协同增强ICB。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a29386aedfab7bd541b2e709\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cc66c3535d922c39c18a7f9d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管临床数据显示肠道菌群组成与ICB疗效相关，但特定共生菌如何具体影响抗肿瘤免疫反应的因果机制尚不明确。特别是，肠道来源的抗原特异性T细胞是否能通过分子模拟识别肿瘤抗原并远程调控肿瘤免疫微环境？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d29c76db287d4902d7d518a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"小鼠模型（C57BL/6J及转基因品系），聚焦肠道共生菌分段丝状菌（SFB）与表达其抗原表位的工程化肿瘤细胞（B16-F10黑色素瘤、LLC1肺癌、MC-38结肠癌）之间的相互作用，评估抗PD-1免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f72242874c5b6a7b09964ec1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在阐明肠道微生物群如何通过分子模拟机制增强免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的抗肿瘤疗效。研究构建了合成新抗原模拟模型，将SFB的一个免疫显性CD4+ T细胞表位（SFB-3340）引入肿瘤细胞。结果显示，仅在SFB定植的小鼠中，抗PD-1治疗能有效抑制表达该抗原的肿瘤生长。通过单细胞测序、谱系追踪和条件性消融实验，研究发现SFB诱导的肠道固有层T_H17细胞迁移至远端肿瘤，在ICB作用下发生表型可塑性，转化为产生IFN-γ和TNF的T_H1-like效应细胞（ex-T_H17）。这些细胞通过重塑肿瘤微环境，促进CD8+细胞毒性T淋巴细胞的招募和活化，从而协同实现肿瘤控制。相比之下，诱导调节性T细胞程序的另一种细菌（H. hepaticus）未能增强ICB疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b6ec471cbe6a6348e28d61eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"治疗后早期（植入后8-12天）给予SFB定植效果最佳，晚期给药效果递减，提示微生物抗原暴露与治疗启动之间存在狭窄的协同时间窗。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::221c27a8f5354ce27eb5e062\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"肿瘤浸润的ex-T_H17细胞表现出类似细胞毒性CD4+ T细胞的基因特征（如Prf1, Klrc1），并在多种人类癌症中被报道与良好预后相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0233dfb9e934c6136eff77e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限于SFB这一特定菌种及与其抗原匹配的肿瘤模型；未涵盖其他常见益生菌或致病菌的作用。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物增强ICI疗效的具体生物学路径：SFB定植通过抗原交叉反应，使肠道T_H17细胞迁移至肿瘤并转化为效应状态，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3549c78bc8da71f89495a609\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制基于合成抗原模型，实际人体内是否存在完全相同的克隆型迁移和表型转换尚需临床数据支持；未涉及髓系细胞或其他免疫细胞的具体贡献细节。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了具体的细胞机制：肠道源性ex-T_H17细胞通过分泌IFN-γ和TNF重塑TME，促进CD8+ TILs的招募和活化；并阐明了CD4+与CD8+ T细胞在微生物辅助的ICI治疗中的协同必要性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::57feddb267d9dc7107db6e17\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅针对Hh这一特定菌种；结果取决于该菌在稳态下诱导调节性T细胞的特性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了阴性对照证据：H. hepaticus虽能诱导抗原特异性T细胞迁移至肿瘤，但因诱导Foxp3+调节性表型而非效应表型，故不能增强ICI疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c2a8592c728805f7c0379757\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究使用的是工程化表达单一微生物抗原片段的肿瘤模型，这种“合成新抗原模拟”可能简化了真实肿瘤微环境中复杂的抗原呈递和T细胞激活过程。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cfa61256c30db627095b2c66\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"结论主要基于小鼠模型，直接外推至人类临床疗效时需考虑物种差异及人类肠道菌群的复杂性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39120ef45f757d09348b3b1a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"SFB在人类肠道中的定植情况和免疫原性与小鼠存在差异，其在人类ICI响应中的确切角色尚属推测，本材料未提供人类队列的直接验证数据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::304b05781116b5c8b54b9c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0388\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e3a78d4894569a6b30fe168f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8fd90b50d682d436bf775d59\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e0a316cc26373fee56f14c01\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d6b0f5be9ac6177edd0917b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性综述方法，综合现有文献，从两个主要维度展开：一是机制层面，分析肠道微生物群及其代谢物如何通过炎症信号、血管生成及特定免疫细胞亚群（如Th17, TAMs, MDSCs, Tregs）的重塑来构建免疫抑制性TME；二是临床转化层面，梳理微生物群特征与ICI及CAR-T疗效关联的证据，并总结基于微生物群的干预策略（如FMT、饮食调整、抗生素管理）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cbc566b73e38d625363c1e7e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群调控肿瘤免疫逃逸的多细胞机制框架，特别是细化了Th17/IL-17轴、TAM极化及PGE2信号在连接微生物与TME中的作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；许多机制描述基于动物模型或相关性研究，因果链条在人体内的普遍性尚待验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7422ea58075663d76f3d7681\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"总结了微生物群组成预测ICI疗效的生物标志物潜力，并列出了具体的有益/有害菌种（如Faecalibacterium, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"不同研究中菌群与疗效的关系存在矛盾（如拟杆菌在不同癌种或疗法下的相反作用），综述指出了这种复杂性但未给出统一的预测规则。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fbcfb3c2ea90da5bc2d1291e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了通过FMT、益生菌、饮食纤维补充及抗生素局部清除等策略优化免疫治疗效果的临床路径。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所提及的干预措施大多处于前临床阶段或小规模临床试验初期，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的支持；摘要未交代具体的检索数据库、时间范围及纳入排除标准。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f86c504ca097bdba4b893e5b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"针对结直肠癌（CRC）模型及人类样本\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定菌群（如具核梭杆菌 F. nucleatum、产肠毒素脆弱拟杆菌 ETBF）通过诱导M2型TAM极化、抑制CD8+ T细胞浸润或激活STAT3通路，促进肿瘤免疫逃逸和进展。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bbdd0c32bab6d639929c4dd7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤小鼠模型及PD-1阻断治疗患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"粪便微生物群移植显示，来自“响应者”的菌群能增强PD-1阻断疗效，增加TME中CD8+ T细胞的活化与浸润；而来自“无响应者”的菌群则无效。双歧杆菌和阿克曼氏菌被证实有助于恢复ICI疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2476a8703a2e47e5d81126fa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CTLA-4阻断治疗模型\",\n          \"finding\": \"某些拟杆菌属（Bacteroides species）通过促进IL-12依赖性的TH1免疫反应增强CTLA-4阻断剂的疗效；但在MSS型CRC中，丰富的拟杆菌可能反而增加Tregs和MDSCs，降低PD-1阻断疗效，显示菌群作用的语境依赖性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1bf0e7e1d636a7829511552\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CAR-T治疗小鼠模型\",\n          \"finding\": \"广谱抗生素使用削弱CAR-T疗效，而万古霉素筛选后的菌群可通过维持IL-12水平增强抗肿瘤T细胞功能；短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）等代谢物通过表观遗传修饰（如抑制HDAC）影响效应分子表达。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e10fc7d8116c7de2c8550055\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e59ae63aefdb6db089c63fe8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"旨在回答肠道微生物群在肿瘤免疫逃逸中扮演的具体角色是什么，以及其组成变化如何导致不同患者对肿瘤免疫治疗产生异质性响应。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a68ec694cfc97e217d5902e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肠道微生物群（Gut Microbiota）及其代谢产物对肿瘤免疫逃逸机制的影响，以及对包括实体瘤在内的多种肿瘤免疫治疗（特别是免疫检查点抑制剂ICIs和CAR-T疗法）疗效的调节作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c3aad0823f6b23360ce0961\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，系统阐述了肠道微生物群如何通过影响肿瘤微环境（TME）中的免疫细胞分化、功能及炎症反应来介导肿瘤免疫逃逸。文章详细讨论了微生物群通过Th17/IL-17轴、肿瘤相关巨噬细胞（TAMs）、髓源性抑制细胞（MDSCs）等途径促进肿瘤进展的机制。此外，综述还评估了肠道微生物群组成如何决定患者对免疫检查点抑制剂（如PD-1/PD-L1和CTLA-4阻断剂）及CAR-T疗法的响应差异，并探讨了通过粪菌移植（FMT）、益生菌、抗生素调控等手段优化微生物群以改善免疫治疗效果的潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::81b09d1bafccd10c6e913027\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了肠道微生物群、肿瘤微环境、免疫逃逸的基本概念，以及微生物-肠-脑/骨/肝轴等跨器官影响的概念。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::53ab6305ca07e640e66b407a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"比较了ICI（PD-1/CTLA-4）与CAR-T疗法受微生物群影响的异同，指出两者均受菌群代谢物和T细胞浸润程度的影响，但具体菌种和作用路径有差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::20347916b13e8652f8a2081f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了抗生素使用（尤其是广谱抗生素）对微生物群破坏及对ICI/CAR-T疗效的负面干扰，并提出了可能的缓解策略（如局部吸附剂、β-内酰胺酶）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d609aff3bf1657c5765dacd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"结论多基于回顾性研究、小样本队列或动物模型；不同癌症类型（如黑色素瘤 vs 结直肠癌）和不同ICI靶点（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）下菌群的作用可能截然不同，不可简单外推。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效的具体证据和方向性结论。指出特定菌群（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、部分拟杆菌）与ICI响应正相关，而另一些情况（如高丰度拟杆菌在MSS-CRC中）可能负相关。同时强调了抗生素滥用对ICI疗效的负面影响。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::42843a4e5e9d7c60de7057bc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"多数机制细节来自小鼠模型（如无菌鼠、人源化鼠）；人体内的确切分子通路（如特定受体TLR2/NLRP3的具体作用）仍需更多临床验证；作者提出的机制多为假设性或相关性解释，非确证性因果证据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物群调节ICI疗效的潜在机制，包括：1）通过代谢物（如肌苷、SCFAs）直接调节T细胞功能；2）通过抗原呈递细胞（DCs）成熟影响T细胞活化；3）通过调节TME中的抑制性细胞（Tregs, MDSCs, M2 TAMs）改变免疫微环境。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0bf8462aa6bbf2b6ff207457\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述涵盖多种肿瘤类型（CRC, HCC, MM, Lung, Pancreatic等），在引用其关于特定机制（如Th17, TAMs）的内容时，需注意区分这些机制是在胃肠道肿瘤还是远处肿瘤中被观察到的，避免将局部机制泛化为所有实体瘤的通用机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1b1b56a5dff5a04297b7215\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的菌群与疗效的关系存在显著的情境依赖性（例如拟杆菌在黑色素瘤中有益，在MSS-CRC中可能有害），使用时必须结合具体的癌症类型和治疗靶点进行限定，不能一概而论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::19d47dfb1039c15190b2b21a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"大量机制描述基于动物实验，人体内的适用性存在不确定性，综述本身也承认许多问题尚未解决，因此在规划综述时应将其视为提出假说和方向的来源，而非确凿的最终结论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::338096c66f3203f121a72c38\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0560\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4436e29bd2eed1ab9dbe\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ebbd06e47ec608eec6da\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-98f83c26a4235fa1de00\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a727ee3f2d2808f7e298f50d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fad0723bcc47590221615cb4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad655126273433bfb8cda448\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de8c10826cd6c3643dd4bf12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作为一篇理论/观点综述，本文采用文献综合与逻辑推演的方法。1. 背景梳理：回顾新抗原特性、中央耐受机制及当前预测算法的不足。2. 机制分析：从TCR识别的特异性与交叉反应性出发，分析新抗原与微生物抗原在序列和结构上的同源性基础。3. 证据整合：汇总关于肠道菌群调节免疫系统、异源免疫现象（heterologous immunity）以及临床样本中新抗原与微生物抗原交叉反应的观察性研究数据。4. 假说构建：基于上述证据，提出“预存异源记忆T细胞是决定新抗原免疫原性的主要因素”这一假说，并讨论其对肿瘤免疫编辑的影响。5. 应用展望：提出将微生物同源性纳入新抗原质量评分模型的构想。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::243e5ba9ef6fb2e0b4a07727\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了一个整合视角：将宿主的微生物暴露史（包括肠道菌群和既往感染）视为影响新抗原免疫原性的关键环境变量，强调了异源记忆T细胞在连接微生物抗原与肿瘤抗原中的作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"这是一篇综述而非实证研究，所提出的机制多为基于现有观察性数据的推论，尚未在大规模前瞻性队列中得到验证；对于不同微生物种类（致病菌vs共生菌）对新抗原免疫原性的具体差异化影响尚不明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::357bf21b9192484994fcfa25\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了当前新抗原预测算法的盲区：忽略了T细胞库的环境塑造因素，建议开发包含微生物序列同源性评分的综合质量模型。\",\n          \"limits\": \"具体的算法实现细节、所需的微生物组数据类型（如物种丰度vs特定菌株存在与否）以及如何量化“同源性贡献”在本文中未提供具体方案，仅作为未来方向提出。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5f0c1a6df76b96cdc6ad0ad4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于Snyder等人及Balachandran等人的临床研究数据\",\n          \"finding\": \"在长期生存的胰腺癌患者中，发现针对新抗原的T细胞同时也能够交叉反应于同源的非癌症微生物抗原（如巨细胞病毒、人乳头瘤病毒等），表明微生物暴露史与新抗原免疫原性存在关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::95344087d6be0ca146dd23ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TCR生物学特性及体外实验证据\",\n          \"finding\": \"TCR具有广泛的交叉反应能力，单个TCR克隆可识别约一百万种不同序列的肽段；新抗原与自身抗原及外源抗原（微生物）在TCR接触位点的相似性决定了其“外来性”程度及免疫原性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c784ff7e97d2fe254cfb134\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"动物模型及临床相关性研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定的肠道菌群（如双歧杆菌、拟杆菌属）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效相关，这种效应部分归因于记忆CD4 T细胞依赖的机制，暗示微生物抗原与新抗原之间的分子模拟可能是ICI起效的机制之一。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3eb6a78519bb85a0873491e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c44bf083a2e77ca5319ba63\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"目前新抗原预测主要依赖HLA结合亲和力，但实际免疫原性较低且个体差异大。现有模型未能充分解释为何某些新抗原能引发强免疫应答而另一些不能。本研究试图解决的核心问题是：宿主的微生物暴露史（特别是通过异源记忆T细胞介导的交叉反应性）如何作为关键因素塑造新抗原的免疫原性？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ecdf8ae009130ae1fd2a9991\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肿瘤新抗原（neoantigens）的免疫原性，宿主微生物群（肠道菌群及既往病原体暴露史）对T细胞应答的影响，以及异源记忆T细胞在其中的作用机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bbb1daa2c675e920fa2d53\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在探讨宿主既往接触的微生物如何通过分子模拟（molecular mimicry）产生异源记忆T细胞，进而影响肿瘤新抗原的免疫原性。文章首先指出传统基于HLA结合预测的新抗原算法存在局限性，且新抗原的实际免疫原性受个体T细胞库影响。随后，文章阐述了T细胞受体（TCR）的交叉反应性特征，即TCR不仅能识别特定抗原，还能识别具有相似三维结构或关键残基的其他肽段。在此基础上，文章提出核心假设：宿主因感染病毒、细菌或接触肠道共生菌而产生的预存异源记忆T细胞，能够通过交叉反应增强对新抗原的识别和应答。文章引用了胰腺癌等实体瘤研究中发现的T细胞交叉反应证据，并讨论了不同微生物种类（如促炎与耐受性菌群）可能带来的不同免疫调节后果。最后，作者建议在未来的新抗原预测算法中纳入微生物暴露史和序列同源性信息，以优化个性化癌症免疫治疗的效果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4eae41ff0c762bde4ae1e16\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章提出应开发包含微生物序列同源性评分的复合新抗原质量模型，认为与微生物抗原同源性高的新抗原更可能具有免疫原性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::88d695772ad853de25e66aef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章指出个体的微生物暴露史（如地区性流行病、饮食习惯导致的菌群差异）会导致预存异源免疫水平的不同，从而影响对新抗原的反应强度。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e243c3dcfe404bbb24d026f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该机制主要基于观察性研究和理论推导，具体到每种微生物是否必然导致更好的疗效，取决于微生物是促炎还是耐受性类型，文中指出这仍是待研究领域。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了详细的分子机制解释：肠道菌群和既往病原体暴露通过产生特异性记忆T细胞，这些T细胞因分子模拟而具备与新抗原交叉反应的能力，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫应答。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e622c6e74321224f12990210\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"文中强调不同研究中鉴定的有效菌群并不完全一致，且这种关联在不同癌症类型和药物间可能存在差异，不能简单外推为所有微生物都增强疗效。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"列举了特定微生物属（如Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia）与ICI（PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4）疗效相关的临床及动物实验证据，并提出了这些微生物可能通过增强新抗原免疫原性来发挥作用的假设。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4c00a94f82f42ab8687a5a20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是综述文章，其提出的“异源记忆T细胞是新抗原免疫原性主要因素”属于作者的观点和假说，并非经过严格因果验证的定论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8f03092b49b02e2d54b6a774\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中引用的微生物与ICI疗效关联的证据来自不同的研究（小鼠模型、人类队列），且涉及的菌种各异，需注意这些关联的情境依赖性，避免将其概括为普适规律。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1ee31a1146b59289bf0e61c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文章重点在于机制探讨，未提供具体的临床干预数据（如补充益生菌是否直接提高新抗原疫苗疗效），因此在规划综述时，应将其定位为机制解释而非干预效果证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3bdb6da52745b0169ec50a55\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0085\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::db10b53b05a00fdea360343b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e55a8c9d389564d56630951\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69b79394d0726b95b6065fa9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1788373d25e3a170db3bb0aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 队列设计：两项前瞻性非随机队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），基于疗效（PFI≥1年）和irAE严重程度（≥2级）将患者分为获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组。采用地标分析（Landmark analysis）以1年为界评估irAE，减少 immortal time bias。2. 多组学分析：宏基因组测序鉴定物种丰度、共现网络、功能通路（如SCFA合成基因）；代谢组GC-MS定量SCFA。3. 分子模拟分析：将微生物序列与自身免疫疾病抗原库及肺癌抗原/抗癌肽数据库比对，识别交叉反应表位。4. 菌株水平分析：使用StrainPhlAn分析大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌的SGBs变异及系统发育信号。5. 外部验证：在McCulloch（黑色素瘤ICI）、Routy（NSCLC ICI）等公共数据集上验证SCFA预测值和抗原模拟结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::27dd931bd58169567e4a4506\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次提供实证证据支持微生物组通过分子模拟驱动irAEs（自身免疫抗原模拟）和ICI疗效（肿瘤抗原模拟）的假设。揭示了长期获益者特有的紧凑微生物网络和丁酸高产能力。明确了菌株水平变异（而非仅物种丰度）对临床表型的决定性作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），可能限制统计效力。抗原模拟分析依赖于公共数据库中的已知表位，可能遗漏未表征的关键表位。菌株分析仅针对丰度较高的少数物种。所有样本为基线采集，无法反映治疗过程中的动态变化。外部验证队列的治疗方案和肿瘤类型不完全一致（如黑色素瘤vs肺癌）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48c7437a9bc25839f3746846\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比获益组与耐药组（宏基因组预测+代谢组验证）\",\n          \"finding\": \"获益组富集丙酸（P=0.01）和丁酸/异丁酸（P=0.12/0.02）。乙酸、丙酸、丁酸水平越高，PFS越长，肿瘤进展风险越低（HR<1, P<0.05）。丁酸生产主要受乙酰辅酶A途径介导。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a4e6d4ef4b3160f0c43baaa5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比irAE组与非irAE组\",\n          \"finding\": \"irAE患者微生物中与系统性红斑狼疮（SLE）、皮肤/结缔组织自身免疫病相关的抗原表位对齐数量更多，特别是在免疫性结肠炎患者中SLE相关表位显著富集（P=0.04）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f2e549ea2a38a11164f7f0ca\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比高疗效组与低疗效组\",\n          \"finding\": \"高疗效组微生物中与肺癌相关的抗原和抗癌肽（ACP）表位对齐数量更多（P=0.07/0.06），并在Routy队列中得到部分验证（P=0.02）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7cfa37c4ed6bd29db16e931a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"特定物种（大肠杆菌、普拉梭菌）\",\n          \"finding\": \"菌株水平变异与临床表型强相关。例如，普拉梭菌SGB15342在获益组中富集，而SGB15323/332_group倾向出现在严重irAE组。不同组间存在高突变率，表明菌株特异性决定功能。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd986072923c2c8b143e0469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1aa6ce49462b4fc36bf4e98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI的初始疗效和irAEs，但其对长期生存获益的具体影响及底层机制（如代谢物、分子模拟、菌株变异）尚不清楚。特别是区分长期获益者与耐药者或仅发生irAE者的微生物特征差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8723f2c5d07d798f6a11ec0f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"中国北京协和医院晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，接受抗PD-1/PD-L1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗。研究聚焦于基线肠道微生物组与代谢组特征对长期疗效（无进展生存期PFI≥1年）及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。样本分为长期获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组，并通过外部公共队列（McCulloch, Routy等）进行验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6739f5f8fdd552af3ccd0592\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组如何影响肺癌患者ICI治疗的长期结局及其潜在机制。通过前瞻性收集基线粪便样本进行宏基因组和代谢组测序，结合临床随访数据，分析微生物组成、短链脂肪酸（SCFA）水平、分子模拟现象及菌株变异与临床表型的关系。研究发现，长期获益患者拥有更紧凑的微生物网络和高产丁酸/丙酸的能力；irAE患者的微生物中存在与自身免疫抗原相似的表位；响应患者的微生物中富含与肺癌抗原相似的表位；且特定物种（如大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌）的菌株水平变异与临床表型显著相关。这些发现为“智能”粪菌移植提供了理论依据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1853254a590326de7a98b136\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"数据主要来自肺癌患者，虽在黑色素瘤队列中验证了丙酸/丁酸趋势，但需注意肿瘤类型的异质性。关联性强，但因果链条需结合其他干预研究理解。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）作为预测ICI长期疗效的生物标志物的实证数据。具体指出丁酸生产依赖乙酰辅酶A途径，且高水平SCFA与延长PFS和降低进展风险相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d439e44dd010530a60fd704\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"分子模拟的证据基于序列同源性比对，属于相关性/预测性证据，尚未通过体内实验直接证明T细胞交叉反应。抗原数据库可能存在偏差。菌株分析仅限于少数物种。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了并初步验证了“分子模拟”机制：1) 微生物抗原模拟宿主自身免疫抗原导致irAEs（特别是SLE相关表位在结肠炎患者中富集）；2) 微生物抗原模拟肿瘤抗原增强ICI疗效。同时强调了菌株特异性（如大肠杆菌毒力基因簇）在决定irAE或耐药中的作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f9084d13af5236dab61bb354\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Co-occurrence networks showing compactness in benefit group; enrichment of butyrate producers like F. prausnitzii, Blautia.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::12d03fe22e6c6021e4b4f5e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion section proposing 'smart' FMT based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdc428f23c1a35942c603cdd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的分子模拟结论是基于生物信息学预测（序列比对），并非直接的免疫学功能验证（如T细胞克隆追踪），在综述中应表述为“提示”或“初步证据”，而非确证机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a15aad3974479b8ec5c7e50f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"菌株水平的发现仅适用于大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌等丰度较高的物种，不能推广到所有微生物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d73df87bb79df88cf488a874\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"外部验证队列（McCulloch, Routy）在肿瘤类型和治疗方案上与主队列存在差异，解读时需考虑肿瘤微环境异质性的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d5f0d5e9220739bab7fe6fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"irAE分析采用了地标分析以校正时间偏倚，这是该方法学上的优势，但在比较不同研究时需注意终点定义的一致性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dba1ca498c98136c62e2487b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-u2gi65cq\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_4e312d3d88\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The specific request for large-scale microbiome association studies focused on non-colitis irAEs (such as myocarditis or neurotoxicity) is not fulfilled by this material. While this study includes some non-colitis irAE cases (e.g., cardiovascular, muscle) within a composite 'severe irAE' group, the total sample size (n=13 for severe irAE) is small, and there is no dedicated large-scale analysis for specific non-colitis subtypes. The authors' own admission of limited sample size confirms the ongoing evidence gap regarding statistical power for specific irAE subtypes.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41eac1d693544443b3b7f8f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a51e25fe21f9f078bc3908f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c9a8ff8f0a39ea5b493d06f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf857de4927d7e4425b19335\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5295b27a17104b3c8d579065\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conduct a narrative review of existing literature. They categorize host factors into four main domains: circulating immune compartment, germline genetics, phenotypic/external features, and gut microbiota. For each domain, they summarize key findings from clinical studies (retrospective analyses, post-hoc trial data, prospective cohorts) and preclinical models (murine studies). They discuss proposed biological mechanisms linking these factors to ICI efficacy, such as immune cell trafficking, antigen presentation, metabolic modulation, and innate immune priming. The review also notes discrepancies in findings across different studies and cancer types, emphasizing the need for validation.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ad79c8cd8f5e794f9d067b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of host-based biomarker candidates beyond tumour tissue, categorizing them into immune, genetic, phenotypic, and microbial domains. Highlights the potential for modifiable factors (diet, microbiome, medications) as targets for combination therapies.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data. Many associations described are based on retrospective analyses or small prospective cohorts, lacking robust validation in large-scale randomized trials. Findings show significant heterogeneity across cancer types and study methodologies, limiting immediate clinical applicability. The review explicitly states that these are candidate biomarkers requiring further validation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::581d07e319b88eadf79d493d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Circulating immune factors\",\n          \"finding\": \"High baseline neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio (NLR) is associated with worse ICI outcomes; eosinophilia is linked to better outcomes. Specific T-cell receptor (TCR) diversity in peripheral PD1+ CD8+ T cells correlates with improved progression-free survival in NSCLC. High IL-8 levels negatively correlate with efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf4c93036684481a24b171e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Germline genetics\",\n          \"finding\": \"HLA-A*03 allele association with poorer OS was not consistently replicated. HLA-I heterozygosity and evolutionary divergence generally associate with better outcomes, though effects vary by cancer type (e.g., HLA-B44 supertype has opposite effects in melanoma vs. NSCLC). FCGR3A V158F SNP associates with improved response to ipilimumab in melanoma.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b3cfba2f8f859a528c563271\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Phenotypic and external features\",\n          \"finding\": \"An 'obesity paradox' exists where higher BMI correlates with better ICI survival in some cancers, potentially mediated by leptin-induced PD1 expression on T cells. High cholesterol also correlates with better anti-PD1 outcomes. Gender effects are controversial. Corticosteroid use (for supportive care) negatively impacts ICI efficacy, while antihistamines may have a positive effect via histamine pathway modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::066a2c2fbd5317027ece5054\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Gut microbiota\",\n          \"finding\": \"Baseline gut microbiota composition and diversity influence ICI efficacy. Specific genera (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) are often positively associated, while others (e.g., Bacteroides eggerthii) are negatively associated, though consensus is lacking due to methodological differences. Mechanisms include production of immunomodulatory metabolites (short-chain fatty acids, inosine), activation of innate immune receptors (NOD2, STING), and molecular mimicry between bacterial and tumour antigens.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2dbc1a4d2e79a33875d890d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::031338a121dcefffb44b207b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To address the unpredictability of tumour responses to ICIs and the limitations of current tumour-centric biomarkers (such as PD-L1, TMB, and MMR deficiency) which require invasive tissue sampling and lack cross-cancer generalizability. The review aims to identify and evaluate host-based factors that could offer better pre-treatment prediction of ICI benefit.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3c83913156da7e0539bfa5a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on host factors influencing the response of patients with solid tumours to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers circulating immune compartments, germline genetic features, phenotypic and external features (exposome), and gut microbial features.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82cc9e6fd19a61ef6fee2b48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This review article synthesizes emerging evidence regarding non-tumour-centric host factors that may serve as predictive biomarkers for ICI efficacy. The authors argue that current FDA-approved biomarkers are limited by their reliance on tumour tissue and poor generalizability across cancer types. Consequently, they explore alternative host-based predictors, including peripheral blood immune markers (e.g., neutrophil-to-lymphocyte ratio, eosinophils, TCR repertoire), germline genetics (e.g., HLA alleles, Fc-gamma receptor polymorphisms), phenotypic traits (e.g., obesity, cholesterol, gender), exogenous factors (e.g., medications like corticosteroids or antibiotics, diet), and specifically the gut microbiota. The paper highlights the potential modifiability of several factors, suggesting avenues for co-therapies to enhance ICI therapeutic index.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c424b1ec5f22edc8c8467b99\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Summaries of circulating immune markers (NLR, eosinophils), germline genetics (HLA, FCGR3A), and phenotypic factors (obesity, cholesterol, gender) and their associations with ICI efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb182cc527a1e60a9482d1ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Evidence that corticosteroids, antibiotics, diet (fibre), and specific medications (antihistamines, beta-blockers) can modulate ICI efficacy, partly through microbiome or immune pathways.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f7d6c0e58b444106855fe1ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of discrepancies in microbiome findings due to differences in stool collection, DNA extraction, sequencing methods (16S vs. shotgun), and bioinformatic pipelines.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6d31f17449d65516fa7cb1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are observational and inconsistent across studies. The review emphasizes that these are correlations, not proven causal relationships for all contexts. Clinical endpoints vary (ORR, PFS, OS).\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Lists specific gut bacterial species and genera (e.g., Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp., Bacteroides eggerthii) that have been associated with positive or negative ICI outcomes in various solid tumour cohorts. Notes the lack of consensus and potential reasons for discrepancies (methodology, geography, cancer type).\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5ce6fafc64a7c4165ef38dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or small human subsets. The review notes that the relative contribution of each mechanism in humans is still being elucidated. Some mechanisms (like butyrate's effect) can be context-dependent (positive for anti-PD1, negative for anti-CTLA4).\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details proposed mechanisms by which gut microbiota influence ICI efficacy: 1) Production of immunomodulatory metabolites (butyrate, inosine, hippurate); 2) Activation of innate immune receptors (NOD2, STING, TLRs) leading to myeloid cell priming and type I interferon production; 3) Molecular mimicry between bacterial epitopes and tumour neoantigens leading to cross-reactive T cells.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b043611ba77b73bd423db17a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers multiple cancer types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, etc.), so findings should not be assumed to apply uniformly to all solid tumours without checking specific context.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec17513be6040007b4b17183\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Microbial associations are highly variable; the review explicitly states there is little consensus on specific species, so any single species mentioned should be treated as a candidate rather than a definitive marker.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6aa91e78c58f0ef496634db8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanisms described are largely hypothetical or based on preclinical models; causal links in humans are not fully established.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f620f751523a363ce2cf08ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative summary, not a systematic meta-analysis; it does not provide pooled effect sizes or rigorous statistical comparisons.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4389546b106d7d8f9c538f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-8c71e871c7aa5482d545\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f85da31c482f020fe5f7\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b67c869eee5a32d72d756c1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::905a16b1317dae09553557fb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4fc1b23aa9738aec8d869909\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"纵向队列研究设计。收集III期黑色素瘤患者在联合ICI治疗前（基线）和治疗后第6周的配对粪便样本（n=126）和外周血PBMC样本（n=71）。使用16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道微生物组成，使用质谱流式细胞术全面 profiling 循环免疫细胞亚群。比较基线与第6周的微生物和免疫指标变化，并分析其与临床应答状态及irAEs严重程度的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ddc7133862b1e98dee7bbcc4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向证据，表明肠道微生物组（特别是拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与ICI治疗期间的免疫细胞动态（特别是Tregs）及临床结局（应答和irAEs）存在关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正）、微生物功能推断细节、以及是否控制了其他混杂因素（如抗生素使用、饮食等）。此外，作为会议摘要，缺乏完整的实验细节和长期随访数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ced063ef4d895bb2527ef3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI治疗前后对比\",\n          \"finding\": \"治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞（Tem）频率增加（P=0.0096）和调节性T细胞（Tregs）频率减少（P=0.0029）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::df0c22db80cc042e49db6078\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据临床应答分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"Tregs的减少主要在应答者中观察到（P=0.0016），而在非应答者中无显著变化（P=0.9515）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::155a4a53fa9c96215b2c32fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据irAEs严重程度分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"发生严重irAEs的患者在第6周时Tregs显著缺乏（P=0.0293），相比无或轻度毒性患者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4dd917c890edeb09e25c7941\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与免疫变化的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"在循环Tregs减少的患者中，Tregs减少的程度与基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）相对丰度呈正相关（P<0.0001）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43564e4cabb74c63d54ecf12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与临床结局的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的基线拟杆菌属丰度与更严重的irAEs发展（P=0.0472）及第6周前更高的类固醇使用率（P=0.0345）相关。相反，较高的瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）丰度具有保护作用，且瘤胃球菌科主导的微生物组患者中应答者比例更高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b30b98ec45be93bfcf01d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b52da9c89aaeaaa5b0749b6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，但具体机制不明。本研究试图解决：肠道微生物如何与免疫系统相互作用以影响ICI的成功或irAEs的发生？特别是特定细菌类群（如拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与免疫细胞亚群变化及临床结局之间的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15613d5b09de0b9d50378597\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"III期黑色素瘤患者，接受新辅助联合抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；涉及澳大利亚和荷兰队列（n=126），其中71名患者有匹配的PBMC数据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e128a47c0a17f95654887c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组与免疫系统在ICI治疗中的纵向动态关系及其对疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。通过对126名患者的基线和第6周粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序，并对71名患者的外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）进行质谱流式细胞术分析，研究发现ICI治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞增加和调节性T细胞（Tregs）减少。Tregs的减少主要见于应答者，但在发生严重irAEs的患者中也观察到显著缺乏。基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与Tregs减少程度及严重irAEs风险正相关，而瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用并关联更好的应答。结论指出肠道微生物组可能通过影响免疫平衡的“临界点”来塑造ICI的治疗结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46fff116fb877592fe07c91f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅针对III期黑色素瘤患者，且为新辅助联合ICI治疗情境；不能直接外推至其他肿瘤类型或单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌类群（拟杆菌属、瘤胃球菌科）与ICI疗效（客观缓解）及毒性（irAEs严重程度）的具体关联方向和数据支持。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ba5a4a521ab5b76c9cdd393\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察性关联提出的假设性机制（'suggests that...'），并非经过功能验证的因果机制；需结合其他研究确认其普遍性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制线索：肠道微生物组可能通过影响基线免疫稳态（特别是Tregs的水平）来设定免疫反应的‘阈值’或‘临界点’，从而影响抗肿瘤免疫和irAEs的发生。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bed1c5a92a1c909e5a7e55ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"摘要中提到‘how gut microbes interact with the immune system... remains unclear’，反映了该领域的知识空白和研究动机。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5fb91d23ecba19c99dc65b1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"拟杆菌属既与Treg减少（通常关联疗效）相关，又与严重irAEs相关；而瘤胃球菌科则显示保护性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::561b8cc96f7980e0b68fb9a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为会议摘要，详细的方法学细节（如测序深度、生物信息学流程、流式抗体面板、统计分析模型）未在摘要中提供，需谨慎引用具体数值和方法论细节。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e79b3405bb023182accfa755\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象仅限于III期黑色素瘤患者，且接受的是新辅助联合ICI治疗，结果可能不适用于晚期转移性黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fee2de282937a619aa2bdca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关联不等于因果：观察到的微生物与免疫细胞及临床结局的关联可能是由其他未测量的混杂因素驱动的，或反映的是反向因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7929958b24e5e4211328f19b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"‘拟杆菌属’是一个属水平的分类单元，其内部物种可能存在功能差异，摘要未提供更精细的分类或功能信息。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e1908b8bbd498777e918ecb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a124c25a896c4263a63a816d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9120e5406f330dcaca180bb4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1b3b78fff1cfd7128085c82\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作为一篇综述，本研究未进行新的实验数据采集，而是通过系统性文献回顾，整合了关于皮肤微生物组组成、空间异质性、免疫调节机制以及临床干预措施的多学科证据。作者将材料组织为：1) 皮肤共生菌的组成与空间分布；2) 共生菌在免疫稳态中的作用机制；3) AD的免疫特征与失衡；4) 菌群-免疫-屏障的恶性循环；5) 基于微生物组的临床应用与未来疗法。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a05ab0f6a4ed411ae24a7f5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了AD病理中“菌群-免疫-屏障”三角关系的综合机制框架，特别是明确了共生菌代谢物（SCFAs, 色氨酸衍生物）对AHR和HDAC通路的调控作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及质量评价方法；部分机制描述基于动物模型或体外研究，其在人体内的确切效力尚需更多临床数据验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::741772badca9ce611340d694\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"健康皮肤 vs AD皮损\",\n          \"finding\": \"AD皮损中金黄色葡萄球菌（S. aureus）绝对丰度显著增加并与疾病严重程度正相关，而共生菌（如S. epidermidis, C. acnes）丰度降低，导致多样性下降（Shannon指数降低40-60%）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c087ac177d0a23542443077\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"共生菌免疫调节机制\",\n          \"finding\": \"S. epidermidis通过分泌抗菌肽抑制S. aureus，并通过TLR2信号诱导IL-1β/IL-6促进Th17分化同时上调Foxp3增强Treg功能；色氨酸代谢物（如IAId）作为AHR配体抑制TSLP表达，从而减轻Th2炎症。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::679eb1daad55b087013bfa25\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肠道-皮肤轴干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"口服特定益生菌（如Limosilactobacillus fermentum SLAM216或Bifidobacterium组合）可降低儿童AD患者的SCORAD评分，机制涉及增加粪便短链脂肪酸浓度及调节肠道菌群比例。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b1f0eb2fe91c950f3e6dd66\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"传统疗法局限性与新疗法潜力\",\n          \"finding\": \"Dupilumab虽有效但存在潜在淋巴瘤风险；靶向微生物组的疗法（如自体S. hominis A9菌株、噬菌体、内溶素）在早期临床试验中显示出修复屏障和抑制炎症的潜力，但仍处于Phase I/II阶段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c446a679f2e091a0d075ff1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fd8eb8d8a18c05467339f07\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"旨在解决传统AD疗法（如糖皮质激素、生物制剂）长期使用的副作用及无法根治免疫失衡的问题，探索通过调节皮肤及肠道微生物组来恢复免疫稳态的新机制和治疗途径。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::549c0bca352d7608049f51f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"特应性皮炎（AD）患者的皮肤微生态、宿主免疫反应及皮肤屏障功能之间的相互作用；涉及肠道-皮肤轴在AD发病机制中的潜在角色。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04e9a73dca7588ad83f3ad87\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，系统分析了皮肤共生菌与宿主免疫系统在特应性皮炎（AD）稳态维持与失衡中的作用。文章首先阐述了皮肤微生物群的空间分布及其组成变化，指出金黄色葡萄球菌（S. aureus）的富集和共生菌（如表皮葡萄球菌 S. epidermidis）的减少是AD皮损的特征。接着，详细探讨了共生菌通过代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs、色氨酸代谢物）、抗菌肽分泌及受体信号通路（如TLR2、AHR）调节Th1/Th2/Th17免疫平衡的机制。文章进一步描述了“菌群失调-免疫激活-屏障破坏”的恶性循环，并评估了基于益生菌、益生元、噬菌体及粪菌移植等靶向微生物组的新型治疗策略的临床潜力与传统疗法的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f8081b65be3ae1ee4455eac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中关于共生菌（如S. epidermidis）通过TLR2信号诱导Treg分化，以及色氨酸代谢物通过AHR通路抑制Th2炎症的描述。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::484d18ae40eebafc80220a66\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中提到的益生菌（L. fermentum）、益生元、噬菌体和自体细菌移植在AD中的早期临床试验结果（如SCORAD评分改善）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29fbf81a5950559cf7f1ac3a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"研究对象为皮肤和肠道微生物，疾病为AD而非癌症；涉及的免疫通路主要为Th2/Th17/Treg，与ICI相关的CD8+ T细胞耗竭或激活机制不同。不能直接外推至ICI疗效预测。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组调节适应性免疫（特别是T细胞亚群极化）的详细机制案例。具体展示了共生菌如何通过代谢物（SCFAs, 色氨酸衍生物）和表面分子（PSA, LTA）影响DC细胞活化及Treg/Th17平衡。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::80e0594fb6192c6dbcbb085c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些机制是在AD炎症背景下描述的，重点在于抗炎和屏障修复，而非抗肿瘤免疫监视。具体分子通路（如JAK-STAT, STAT6）与ICI的主要效应通路（PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4）无直接重叠。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐述了微生物代谢物（如SCFAs）通过表观遗传修饰（HDAC抑制）和受体信号（GPR43, AHR）调节免疫细胞功能的分子机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f98a4601fa400af7e7804c34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文研究对象为特应性皮炎（AD），非实体瘤。其涉及的免疫机制（Th2主导）与ICI治疗中关注的抗肿瘤免疫（通常涉及Th1/CD8+ T细胞）存在显著差异，不可直接套用结论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c5f1e5c0bc588c23fb79a36\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的肠道-皮肤轴机制主要基于AD背景下的观察，其与肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体连接点（如特定菌属、代谢物）在本材料中未明确建立，需谨慎推断。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9356ec5b54d3437f4a20b895\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"部分机制（如AHR通路、SCFA作用）在AD中已被详细描述，但在ICI语境下是否同样关键，需结合其他专门针对肿瘤的研究进行验证，本材料仅提供平行领域的机制参考。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9bd9ead8f11ec34694ca7302\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0154\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b89bdc41d869f6a97b20\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-582f20ac7ee4be08eea3\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cf4c1b6e827b39baa70b33a9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c22d57fd87eb086735879a57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9ad756960631cbf08b0bdfba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::888e46cf068a669f02f24630\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"体内实验：建立B16.OVA黑色素瘤和Panc02胰腺癌皮下移植模型。设置对照组、DAT单药组、ICI单药组及DAT+ICI联合组。引入广谱抗生素（Abx）混合液饮水处理以诱导肠道菌群失调，评估DAT对菌群失调导致的ICI抵抗的补偿作用。使用Ifnar1-/-小鼠验证宿主IFN-I信号在DAT介导的免疫增强中的必要性。体外实验：分离脾脏T细胞和骨髓来源树突状细胞（DC），在TCR刺激或LPS共刺激条件下，检测DAT对细胞活化标志物（如CD25, IFNγ, CD80/86）的影响。分析手段包括流式细胞术（TME免疫细胞图谱）、16S-rRNA测序（肠道菌群组成变化）、靶向代谢组学（粪便DAT水平测定）及生存分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7dd61fd659b69e3af70bbfb8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"识别了细菌代谢物DAT作为IFN-I调节剂，能够协同ICI增强抗肿瘤T细胞免疫的具体表型和机制依赖关系。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代DAT在体内的确切受体或上游感知机制；仅在小鼠模型中验证，尚未在人类临床试验中证实安全性和有效性；DAT对菌群组成的改变是因果还是伴随现象尚不明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::985c2cbb806631682ca1d391\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"B16.OVA黑色素瘤模型 + 抗CTLA-4治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"口服DAT显著延迟肿瘤生长并提高长期生存率，表现为肿瘤微环境（TME）中IFNγ+ CD4+和CD8+ T细胞以及NK细胞的频率和活性增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05f735350695e36e26a7cb93\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Ifnar1-/-小鼠模型 + 抗CTLA-4治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"DAT的协同增效作用完全消失，表明DAT增强ICI疗效严格依赖于宿主完整的IFN-I信号通路。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd731b745b7c3e483c2547\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::165122414afb942c2406b476\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"广谱抗生素（Abx）诱导的菌群失调模型 + 抗CTLA-4治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"虽然DAT不能阻止抗生素引起的肠道细菌耗竭，但能部分恢复抗CTLA-4的抗肿瘤疗效，延长生存期，并促进循环中抗原特异性T细胞的扩增。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f4dd7